The non-scope-hoisting packager creates one new asset per non-JS dependency resolution, while this currently returns a new `{}` for every single use of that dependency:

```js
const x = require("./index.css");
console.log(x);
console.log(x);
```
becomes
```js
console.log({});
console.log({});
```

